31 CFR 1010.670	FinCEN	1 obligation(s)	3 rule(s)
	High	1010.670 — Comply with FinCEN/Treasury summons or subpoena requests for records relating to a correspondent account maintained for a foreign bank, and terminate the correspondent relationship within the required timeframe if directed.	
			[REGULATORY] Institution must produce records relating to a foreign correspondent account within 7 days of receiving a summons or subpoena  · evidence: Legal/subpoena response tracker
			[REGULATORY] Correspondent relationship must be terminated within 10 business days of receiving written notice from FinCEN/Treasury of failure to comply  · evidence: Correspondent banking offboarding procedure
			[BUSINESS] Escalation path for a failure-to-terminate scenario must be defined and periodically tested  · evidence: Escalation procedure documentation
31 CFR 1020.210	FinCEN	7 obligation(s)	20 rule(s)
	Critical	1020.210 — Maintain a written AML compliance program approved by the board of directors and noted in the board minutes.	
			[REGULATORY] A current written AML program document must exist  · evidence: Policy repository
			[REGULATORY] Board approval of the AML program must be evidenced in minutes within the last 12 months  · evidence: Board minutes
			[BUSINESS] Program must be reviewed by the BSA officer at least annually  · evidence: Review log
			[TECHNICAL] Policy document version and approval date must be machine-readable  · evidence: Policy metadata
	Critical	1020.210 — Establish a system of internal controls to assure ongoing BSA compliance.	
			[REGULATORY] Documented internal controls must exist for each BSA reporting obligation  · evidence: Control library
			[BUSINESS] Each control must have a named owner and test frequency  · evidence: Control library
	Critical	1020.210 — Provide for independent testing of BSA compliance by qualified internal or external personnel.	
			[REGULATORY] Independent BSA testing must have been performed within the last 12 months  · evidence: Audit reports
			[REGULATORY] Tester must be independent of the BSA function being tested  · evidence: Engagement record
			[BUSINESS] Findings from independent testing must be tracked to closure  · evidence: Issue tracker
	Critical	1020.210 — Designate an individual responsible for coordinating and monitoring day-to-day BSA compliance.	
			[REGULATORY] A designated BSA officer must be named and board-appointed  · evidence: Board minutes
			[BUSINESS] BSA officer designation must be re-confirmed on personnel change  · evidence: HR record
	High	1020.210 — Provide training for appropriate personnel on BSA requirements.	
			[REGULATORY] BSA training must be completed by all applicable staff within the last 12 months  · evidence: LMS records
			[REGULATORY] Training content must be role-appropriate for the functions performed  · evidence: Curriculum record
			[BUSINESS] New hires in covered roles must complete BSA training within 30 days  · evidence: LMS records
			[TECHNICAL] Completion rate metric = completed / assigned * 100  · evidence: LMS export
	Critical	1020.210 — Maintain appropriate risk-based procedures for ongoing customer due diligence.	
			[REGULATORY] Risk-based CDD procedures must be documented in the AML program  · evidence: Policy repository
			[REGULATORY] Each customer must carry a risk rating assigned at onboarding  · evidence: CIF / core system
			[BUSINESS] Risk rating must be refreshed at defined trigger events  · evidence: CIF change log
	High	1020.210 — Conduct and document a BSA/AML risk assessment covering products, services, customers, and geographies.	
			[REGULATORY] A documented BSA/AML risk assessment must exist and be current  · evidence: Risk assessment doc
			[BUSINESS] Risk assessment must be refreshed at least annually or on material change  · evidence: Version history
31 CFR 1020.220	FinCEN	7 obligation(s)	15 rule(s)
	Critical	1020.220(a)(2) — Implement a written Customer Identification Program appropriate for the institution's size and type of business.	
			[REGULATORY] A written CIP must exist and be incorporated into the AML program  · evidence: Policy repository
	Critical	1020.220(a)(2)(i) — Collect name, date of birth (individuals), address, and identification number before opening an account.	
			[REGULATORY] IF account_opened THEN customer_name must be non-null  · evidence: Core / CIF
			[REGULATORY] IF customer_type = individual THEN date_of_birth must be non-null  · evidence: Core / CIF
			[REGULATORY] Physical address must be non-null; a PO box alone is insufficient for individuals  · evidence: Core / CIF
			[REGULATORY] Identification number (TIN/SSN/ITIN, or passport for non-US persons) must be non-null  · evidence: Core / CIF
			[BUSINESS] Account may not be activated until all four CIP elements are captured  · evidence: Account workflow
	Critical	1020.220(a)(2)(ii) — Verify the identity of each customer within a reasonable time using documentary or non-documentary methods.	
			[REGULATORY] A verification method (documentary or non-documentary) must be recorded per customer  · evidence: CIP system
			[REGULATORY] Verification must be completed within the institution's defined reasonable time  · evidence: CIP system
			[BUSINESS] Unverified accounts must be escalated after the defined ageing threshold  · evidence: Exception queue
	High	1020.220(a)(3) — Retain CIP identifying information for five years after the account is closed, and verification records for five years after the record is made.	
			[REGULATORY] CIP identifying information retained 5 years after account closure  · evidence: Archive index
			[REGULATORY] Verification records retained 5 years after the record was made  · evidence: Archive index
			[TECHNICAL] Retention clock field must differ for identifying vs verification records  · evidence: Archive schema
	High	1020.220(a)(4) — Compare each new customer against any federal list of known or suspected terrorists designated for CIP purposes.	
			[REGULATORY] Each new customer must be compared against designated government lists  · evidence: Screening log
	Medium	1020.220(a)(5) — Provide customers with adequate notice that information is being requested to verify their identity.	
			[REGULATORY] CIP notice must be provided and evidence of delivery retained  · evidence: Disclosure system
	Medium	1020.220(b) — Where relying on another financial institution for CIP, obtain the required contract and annual certification.	
			[REGULATORY] IF relying on another FI THEN contract and annual certification must be on file  · evidence: Vendor repository
31 CFR 1020.315	FinCEN	3 obligation(s)	3 rule(s)
	Medium	1020.315(b) — Apply CTR exemptions only to eligible exempt persons under Phase I or Phase II.	
			[REGULATORY] Each exemption must map to a qualifying Phase I or Phase II exempt person category  · evidence: Exemption register
	Medium	1020.315(c) — File a Designation of Exempt Person (DOEP) for each exempted non-listed business or payroll customer.	
			[REGULATORY] A DOEP filing must exist for each Phase II exempt person  · evidence: Filing record
	Medium	1020.315(h) — Review the eligibility of each exempt person at least once each year.	
			[REGULATORY] Each exempt person must have an annual eligibility review within the last 12 months  · evidence: Exemption register
31 CFR 1020.320	FinCEN	9 obligation(s)	20 rule(s)
	Critical	1020.320(b)(3) — File a SAR within 30 calendar days of initial detection of facts constituting a basis for filing.	
			[REGULATORY] IF suspicious_activity_detected THEN SAR_filed_date minus detection_date is 30 calendar days or fewer  · evidence: BSA case system
			[REGULATORY] IF no suspect identified THEN the deadline extends to 60 calendar days  · evidence: BSA case system
			[BUSINESS] Escalate to the BSA officer when a case reaches day 25 unfiled  · evidence: Alerting service
			[TECHNICAL] Detection date must be system-captured, not user-entered  · evidence: Case schema
			[TECHNICAL] IF case query returns zero rows THEN INDETERMINATE, never PASS  · evidence: Evidence connector
			[TECHNICAL] BSA case records retained 5 years and retrievable by subject name  · evidence: Archive index
	Critical	1020.320(a)(2)(i) — File a SAR for insider abuse involving any amount.	
			[REGULATORY] IF insider_abuse_identified THEN SAR required regardless of amount  · evidence: BSA case system
			[TECHNICAL] Insider abuse rule must carry no dollar threshold parameter  · evidence: Rule config
			[BUSINESS] Alert BSA officer at day 100 of the 120-day window  · evidence: Alerting service
	Critical	1020.320(a)(2)(ii) — File a SAR for transactions aggregating $5,000 or more where a suspect can be identified.	
			[REGULATORY] IF aggregate 5000 or more AND suspect identified THEN SAR required  · evidence: BSA case system
	Critical	1020.320(a)(2)(iii) — File a SAR for transactions aggregating $25,000 or more regardless of whether a suspect can be identified.	
			[REGULATORY] IF aggregate 25000 or more THEN SAR required even with no identified suspect  · evidence: BSA case system
	High	1020.320 — File a continuing-activity SAR by the 120-day deadline where suspicious activity persists.	
			[REGULATORY] IF activity continues THEN next SAR filed on or before prior SAR date plus 120 calendar days  · evidence: BSA case system
			[REGULATORY] Review period parameter equals 90 days and filing window equals 30 days  · evidence: Rule config
			[BUSINESS] Alert the BSA team at day 100 of the 120-day window  · evidence: Alerting service
	Critical	1020.320(e) — Do not notify any person involved in the transaction that a SAR has been filed.	
			[REGULATORY] SAR existence must not be disclosed outside permitted recipients  · evidence: Access control log
			[TECHNICAL] SAR records must be access-restricted by role with logged reads  · evidence: IAM / audit log
	High	1020.320(d) — Retain a copy of each SAR and its supporting documentation for five years from the filing date.	
			[REGULATORY] SAR copies and supporting documentation retained 5 years from filing  · evidence: Archive index
	Medium	1020.320(c) — Promptly notify the board of directors, or a committee thereof, of SARs filed.	
			[REGULATORY] Board or committee notification of SAR filings must be evidenced  · evidence: Board minutes
	High	1020.320(b)(2) — Complete all mandatory SAR fields including subject identifiers, activity dates, amounts, and narrative.	
			[REGULATORY] SAR narrative must be non-empty at submission  · evidence: Filing record
			[REGULATORY] Subject identifiers, activity date range, and amount must be populated where known  · evidence: Filing record
