Ch. V	OFAC	3 obligation(s)	13 rule(s)
	Critical	Ch. V — Screen customers and members against the SDN and Consolidated sanctions lists at onboarding.	
			[REGULATORY] Every new customer or member must be screened before account activation  · evidence: Screening log
			[REGULATORY] Screening must cover both the SDN list and the Consolidated non-SDN lists  · evidence: List registry
			[REGULATORY] All known aliases must be included in the match set  · evidence: Screening config
			[TECHNICAL] List version and SHA-256 of the source file must be recorded per screening event  · evidence: Screening audit record
			[BUSINESS] Potential matches must be adjudicated by a second reviewer before release  · evidence: Case system
			[TECHNICAL] List version and SHA-256 of the source file must be recorded per screening event  · evidence: Screening audit record
			[TECHNICAL] IF list_version stale beyond internal SLA THEN raise platform health alert (NOT a regulatory violation)  · evidence: Ingestion monitor
	Critical	Ch. V — Screen transactions, including wire beneficiaries and originators, before release.	
			[REGULATORY] Every wire beneficiary must be screened before release  · evidence: Screening log
			[REGULATORY] Screening must occur before value transfer, not after settlement  · evidence: Wire event sequence
			[BUSINESS] Potential matches must be adjudicated by a reviewer before release  · evidence: Case system
			[TECHNICAL] Fuzzy match threshold must be configured and its value recorded  · evidence: Screening config
	High	Ch. V — Re-screen the existing customer base when sanctions lists are updated.	
			[REGULATORY] Customer base must be re-screened following each sanctions list update  · evidence: Batch screening log
			[TECHNICAL] IF list ingestion stale beyond internal SLA THEN platform health alert, NOT a regulatory violation  · evidence: Ingestion monitor
Guidance	OFAC	1 obligation(s)	2 rule(s)
	Critical	Guidance — Treat any entity owned 50 percent or more, directly or indirectly, individually or in the aggregate, by blocked persons as itself blocked.	
			[REGULATORY] Entities owned 50 percent or more in aggregate by blocked persons must be treated as blocked  · evidence: Ownership screening
			[TECHNICAL] Aggregate ownership must sum across multiple blocked persons, not evaluate each separately  · evidence: Ownership graph
